From e11850f13282a712d25c5e470beb8301197524e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: creative-andrew <andres@netzstrategen.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:58:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard the composited item quantity step against a zero
 parent quantity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Loading any page that renders an add-to-cart block while a composite sits in
the cart throws `DivisionByZeroError: Division by zero` and takes the whole page
down with WordPress's critical error screen (ID-998). The trace runs
ProductButton -> BlocksSharedState::load_cart_state() -> Hydration -> this
filter, so it is not confined to the cart page.

`$step` is the composited item's own `multiple_of`, which
filter_container_cart_item_quantity_limits() derives from the parent composite's
cart quantity. A zero parent quantity leaves it at zero, and on PHP 8 dividing
by it is fatal rather than the warning it was on PHP 7.

The vendor already fixed exactly this in 11.0.6 — "Prevented division-by-zero
warnings when normalizing composited cart item quantities against a zero parent
quantity" — but only in the classic cart path, class-wc-cp-cart.php:1861. The
Store API path it missed is the one the Cart and Checkout blocks use, so the
bug only surfaced once the shop moved to block checkout. This applies the same
guard there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 includes/api/class-wc-cp-store-api.php | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/includes/api/class-wc-cp-store-api.php b/includes/api/class-wc-cp-store-api.php
index bd8056e6a..9c2f60c0a 100644
--- a/includes/api/class-wc-cp-store-api.php
+++ b/includes/api/class-wc-cp-store-api.php
@@ -464,7 +464,9 @@ class WC_CP_Store_API {
 		if ( $max ) {
 			// Limit child item max quantity.
 			$item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum = min( $item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum, $max );
-			$item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum = floor( $item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum / $step ) * $step;
+			if ( $step > 0 ) {
+				$item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum = floor( $item_data['quantity_limits']->maximum / $step ) * $step;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
